# Mnemosyne cron stack — box USER crontab reference artifact
# =============================================================================
# This is a REFERENCE FILE, NOT an installed crontab. See README.md (same dir)
# for the install procedure. A single integration pass appends the lines you
# actually want to the live `crontab -e` after review — do NOT pipe this whole
# file into `crontab <file>` (it would clobber whatever else is already there).
#
# Pattern: box-cron-primary (this stack runs on whatever box hosts your
# Mnemosyne MCP servers). Hygiene on every job:
#   flock -n (no overlap) + timeout (hang ceiling) + staggered minute
#   (no two jobs share a minute; nothing on :00 or :30).
# Auth: if you invoke `claude -p` from a job, run it with whatever env forces
# your subscription/OAuth auth rather than an API key, if that's your setup.
# =============================================================================

# CRON_TZ — set to your timezone. Shown here only so this artifact is
# self-describing — check your existing crontab before re-adding it.
CRON_TZ=UTC

# --- Placeholders to replace before using any line below ---------------------
#   /path/to/your/project        -> your project's working-tree path
#   PROJECT_REPO_ID               -> the repo id this project is indexed under
#                                    in the codebase MCP (env var read by
#                                    mnemo-reindex.sh)
#   MNEMOSYNE_COMPOSE_DIR          -> where the Mnemosyne stack's compose file
#                                    lives (env var read by mnemo-reindex.sh)

# --- Mnemosyne cron stack — APPEND the lines you want to `crontab -e` --------

# Job A — codebase MCP incremental re-index (data-plane; NO claude -p).
# Reads /repos:ro, re-embeds only files whose content_sha256 changed.
# Run this before anything that consumes a fresh index (e.g. a distillation job).
40 3 * * * MNEMOSYNE_COMPOSE_DIR=/opt/mnemosyne PROJECT_REPO_ID=your-repo-id flock -n /tmp/mnemo-reindex.lock -c '/path/to/your/project/.claude/scripts/cron/mnemo-reindex.sh' >> $HOME/.mnemo-reindex.log 2>&1

# Job B (optional) — rule-distillation loop (claude -p; the learned-rules loop).
# Body: .claude/scripts/mnemosyne/distill.sh. Must run AFTER the codebase reindex
# (Job A) if the distiller ever consumes the code index, and needs DATABASE_URL
# set to your project's own Postgres (see docs/LearnedRulesLoop.md).
# 15 5 * * * flock -n /tmp/mnemo-distill.lock -c 'DATABASE_URL=postgres://... /path/to/your/project/.claude/scripts/mnemosyne/distill.sh' >> $HOME/.mnemo-distill.log 2>&1

# Job C (optional) — weekly promotion digest for the learned-rules loop.
# Body: .claude/scripts/mnemosyne/weekly-digest.sh.
# 0 9 * * 1 flock -n /tmp/mnemo-digest.lock -c 'DATABASE_URL=postgres://... /path/to/your/project/.claude/scripts/mnemosyne/weekly-digest.sh' >> $HOME/.mnemo-digest.log 2>&1
# --- end Mnemosyne cron stack ------------------------------------------------

# --- Example slot map (adapt to your own schedule) ---------------------------
#   40 3        codebase reindex           (Job A)
#   15 5        rule-distillation          (Job B, optional)
#   09 9 (Mon)  promotion digest           (Job C, optional)
# No two jobs should share a minute; avoid :00/:30 if other cron on the box
# already lands there.
